{"text": "COMMONWEALTH OF VIRGINIA\n\nHOUSE OF DELEGATES\n\nRICHMOND\n\nFebruary 21, 2013\n\nThe Honorable Lacy E. Putney\nGeneral Assembly Building\nRoom 947\nRichmond, VA 23219\n\nThe Honorable Walter A. Stosch\nGeneral Assembly Building\nRoom 626\nRichmond, VA 23219\n\nDear Chairman Putney and Chairman Stosch,\n\nWe are writing to urge the budget conferees to support the Senate language for Medicaid expansion.\nThe Senate language provides the appropriate safeguards that insist on state flexibility and robust\nreforms, as well as assurances that the promised Federal match remains.\n\nThe House language, however, presents significant hurdles to expansion that will result in a delay of 18\nmonths at a loss of $3 billion to our economy. Virginia's hospitals, clinics and physician offices will feel\nthe direct impact, of which could be devastating to many jobs. In addition, taxpayers will still have to pay\nfor other states expansion without any benefit to our economy. Finally, there are nearly 300,000 poor\nuninsured Virginians that are counting on Medicaid expansion that should not have to unnecessarily\nwait those 18 months.\n\nFor those reasons, we believe the Senate language is far superior and the most fiscally and prudently\nresponsible. Our economy cannot afford to lose out on $3 billion. And we simply cannot support a\nbudget that doesn't expand Medicaid.\n\nSincerely,\n\na",
